摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"在 Web 界面进行分支切换与 git worktree 隔离的 DSH 插件","id":"gh:1335625892","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-git-worktree","slug":"LaoYueHanNi/dsh-git-worktree","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"在 Web 界面进行分支切换与 git worktree 隔离的 DSH 插件"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-git-worktree"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"简体中文 | English"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A dsh plugin for simple branch & worktree management in the Web UI. The composer tool row shows the "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"current branch: pick another to switch in place, or flip the **Worktree** toggle to get an isolated "},{"id":"p4s3","text":"worktree as a real workspace — as shown in the screenshot above."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Repo: <https://github.com/LaoYueHanNi/dsh-git-worktree>"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **GitHub direct installs have ended** — the repository no longer carries prebuilt o"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"utput. Install from npm instead:\n>\n[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":">\n> **Upgrading from a legacy `github:` install (≤ 0.3.2, package name `dsh-git-worktree`)?** An in-"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"place `update` fails to load — remove the old name first, then add again. Worktree folders and the p"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"lugin's settings carry over untouched."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- **Commit graph**: expand the branch popup in place to browse branches on the left and their real c"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ommit history and merge graph on the right. Browsing does not check out a branch. Select a commit to"},{"id":"p9s3","text":" see its author, date, full message and file summary; bodies start with a three-line preview and exp"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"and into an internally scrolling area. History loads the next page when its list scrolls to the end,"},{"id":"p9s5","text":" and a Load more button remains; search covers loaded titles and hashes. The author menu lists every"},{"id":"p9s6","text":" author on the branch and keeps that list in memory for the commit; a branch update, fetch, or reloa"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"d drops the cache.\n- **IDEA-style branch picker**: the branch menu treats `/` as a folder hierarchy "},{"id":"p9s8","text":"— collapsible folders, last-segment labels, the checked-out branch's chain opens centered. Local and"},{"id":"p9s9","text":" remote branches render as two collapsible groups (a single remote strips its prefix), with bottom s"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"earch (ancestor folders kept, hits highlighted), locate-current-branch and expand/collapse tools, an"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"d green ↗N / blue ↙N divergence marks on tracking branches.\n- **Remote branch checkout**: pick `orig"},{"id":"p9s12","text":"in/feat-x` in the remote group and it checks out in place with a tracking branch directly (no confir"},{"id":"p9s13","text":"mation); the worktree toggle sends the pick to an isolated worktree instead.\n- **Row context menu**:"},{"id":"p9s14","text":" right-click a branch row for six verbs — check out (immediate, no confirmation), new branch, new br"},{"id":"p9s15","text":"anch and check out, rename branch (local rows), delete branch (local rows, the safe `-d`: git refuse"},{"id":"p9s16","text":"s unmerged commits and occupied branches), copy branch; a worktree row offers go-to-worktree, copy p"},{"id":"p9s17","text":"ath, and remove worktree. Second-level dialogs open IN PLACE of the menu; in-place actions keep the "},{"id":"p9s18","text":"menu open, so rows can be acted on in a run. Keyboard: arrow keys + Enter.\n- **Worktree quick hop**:"},{"id":"p9s19","text":" the main checkout's blank-session menu groups branches held by live worktrees under **Worktrees** ("},{"id":"p9s20","text":"hover shows the directory) — the row menu's \"Go to this worktree\" hops straight into that directory "},{"id":"p9s21","text":"and starts a fresh session.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"> The package declares `dsh.bundle`, so `add` wires the plugin into the profile's layer stack automa"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"tically — no config editing needed. Requires the `web` profile (`dsh web`) and a dsh **0.2.0-rc.1** "},{"id":"p12s3","text":"fig editing needed. Requires the `web` profile (`dsh web`) and a dsh **0.2.0-rc.1** (or later) host."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Running a dsh **0.1.2 alpha** host? Install the dedicated compatibility build instead:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"> `@dsh-alpha` is a dist-tag resolving to the latest alpha-host compatibility build (currently `0.4."},{"id":"p15s2","text":"3-dsh-0.1.2-alpha.5`) with peers pinned to the alpha line — a plain `update` never mixes the two cha"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"nnels. On 0.2.0-rc.1 or later, use the default line above."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Update"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Remove"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Worktree folders are kept at both locations (the per-repository `.dsh/gitworktree` layouts and the l"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"egacy central root); the plugin's own settings live in the dsh settings document."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Build once, install a symlink, iterate:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Rebuild and restart `dsh web` to apply changes (`pnpm watch:client` in the plugin directory hot-relo"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ads the client). No `prepare` script by design — `lib/` never enters the repo; `pnpm publish` builds"},{"id":"p24s3","text":" it fresh into the tarball."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Temporary host-only mount (this launch only, no profile changes): create a `cordis.yml` next to the "},{"id":"p25s2","text":"repo pointing at the built host half (Windows needs the `file:///` form), then launch with it:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Only the host half mounts in this mode (the `/plugin/git-worktree/*` routes keep working); for UI wo"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"rk use the `link:` install above."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
